### Pruebas de la API (extensión "REST Client" de VS Code, o copiar a Postman)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
# Pegá acá el token que devuelve el login (solo la parte después de "Bearer ")
@token = PEGAR_TOKEN

### Login OK -> 200 + token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@techlab.com",
  "password": "TU_PASSWORD"
}

### Login con credenciales incorrectas -> 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@techlab.com",
  "password": "incorrecta"
}

### Login sin datos -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Listar productos -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products

### Obtener producto por id -> 200 / 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/ID_DEL_PRODUCTO

### Crear producto (con token) -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/create
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Auriculares gamer",
  "description": "Sonido 7.1, micrófono desmontable",
  "price": 42999.5,
  "stock": 12,
  "category": "Audio"
}

### Crear producto con datos inválidos -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/create
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "price": -10
}

### Crear producto sin token -> 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/create
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sin token",
  "price": 1,
  "stock": 1,
  "category": "Test"
}

### Crear producto con token inválido -> 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products/create
Authorization: Bearer token-falso
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Token falso",
  "price": 1,
  "stock": 1,
  "category": "Test"
}

### Actualizar producto (con token) -> 200 / 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/ID_DEL_PRODUCTO
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 39999,
  "stock": 8
}

### Eliminar producto (con token) -> 200 / 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/ID_DEL_PRODUCTO
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Ruta inexistente -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/no-existe
